WEBVTT

00:00:04.540 --> 00:00:15.250
in the lives of men and nations one quarter of one hour 15 minutes is a tiny span of time yet

00:00:15.250 --> 00:00:21.520
15 minutes is time enough for many things to happen perhaps it is enough time to measure

00:00:21.520 --> 00:00:29.390
the distance between office and home it is enough time for a moment of worship it is enough time

00:00:29.390 --> 00:00:29.970
for a beat

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:36.330
It is enough time for recreation, enough time to end something.

00:00:37.730 --> 00:00:43.350
Fifteen minutes is one thing in times of peace, another in time of war.

00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:56.710
In the event of war, an enemy would have to destroy our strategic forces, our tactical forces, our cities, and our people on one attack.

00:00:57.410 --> 00:00:59.970
And the chances are that the enemy would strike us from the...

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:07.600
north to those responsible for the defense of our civilization 15 minutes could be the priceless

00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:14.120
interim between the first alarm of approaching enemy missiles and the counter-strike of our own

00:01:14.120 --> 00:01:20.840
forces to get this 15 minutes of warning time the united states has formed a partnership with the

00:01:20.840 --> 00:01:27.140
members of the free world, a partnership that guards the transpolar route against attack.

00:01:46.920 --> 00:01:52.910
Arctic is one of the most forbidding territories on the earth. Looking in any direction, you get

00:01:52.910 --> 00:01:59.900
the feeling that man does not belong on this icy rim of the world. The evidence is all around. The vast

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:29.980
The emptiness. The loneliness. The glow of unnatural colors. The extremes of soundlessness. Soundlessness that fills the intervals between screaming wind. Winds that can whip snow into drifts higher than a barn in minutes. For about three months in the Arctic winter, the sun does not rise. And for four months in the summer, it does not set. Temperature.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:37.920
rise to only some 65 degrees in that brief summer moment and dip to 65 degrees below zero for

00:02:37.920 --> 00:02:46.780
seemingly an endless winter but startling as it may be men have been living in the arctic fighting

00:02:46.780 --> 00:02:53.040
the cold the winds the darkness for thousands of years and now to guard us against possible

00:02:53.040 --> 00:02:59.800
attack over the pole modern men men from cities like dallas in atlanta men from states like

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:04.660
and New York. Men from Denmark and the United States have learned also to live

00:03:04.660 --> 00:03:12.400
in the Arctic. They have moved in to build, maintain, and operate the most

00:03:12.400 --> 00:03:20.520
spectacular warning systems in the world. Warning systems that will track the

00:03:20.520 --> 00:03:24.800
paths of intercontinental ballistic missiles and the flights of manned

00:03:24.800 --> 00:03:29.140
bombers. Among the electronic eyes of the North that never close

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:34.960
are the great radars of the Ballistic Missile Early Warning System, called BMEWS.

00:03:36.140 --> 00:03:41.270
This system is maintained by Radio Corporation of America through Air Force contract.

00:03:42.320 --> 00:03:47.800
Each big detection radar of BMEWS is larger than a football field standing on its side,

00:03:48.790 --> 00:03:53.990
and the tracking antenna is housed in a protective radome 140 feet in diameter.

00:03:54.900 --> 00:03:58.680
The complete installation is as tall as a 15-story building.

00:03:59.400 --> 00:03:59.960
These...

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:09.770
radars are among the greatest construction feats in history, and they can detect an object as small

00:04:09.770 --> 00:04:18.050
as a house door at a range of 1,500 nautical miles. This is roughly the distance from Washington, D.C.

00:04:18.430 --> 00:04:25.460
to El Paso, Texas. The BMU's radars send out carefully calibrated beams of pulsed radar energy

00:04:25.460 --> 00:04:27.740
at two elevations above the Earth.

00:04:30.830 --> 00:04:34.910
These form two horizontal detection fans, one above the other.

00:04:36.060 --> 00:04:42.190
If a missile passes through the lower fan, radar pulses bounce back from it and its position is detected.

00:04:44.260 --> 00:04:47.200
Seconds later, the missile will pass through the upper fan.

00:04:50.330 --> 00:04:59.410
From these two points, track, velocity, and impact area are instantly and automatically figured by the BMU's electronic computer.

00:05:03.840 --> 00:05:12.770
Their electronic memory systems store recollections of every missile, spacecraft, or piece of satellite debris that has come within its range.

00:05:18.840 --> 00:05:28.070
There are three BMU sites. The Thule Greenland site is linked with one in Filingdale's Moor, England, and another in Clear, Alaska.

00:05:30.380 --> 00:05:35.740
The BMU site at Clear, Alaska is in an isolated area northeast of Mount McKinley.

00:05:36.540 --> 00:05:41.540
This site provides the detection capability for the west side of the United States and Canada,

00:05:42.360 --> 00:05:45.800
overlapping the edge of the radar originating from Thule, Greenland.

00:05:47.090 --> 00:05:51.070
The Thule site is on the very edge of the treacherous Greenland ice cap,

00:05:52.150 --> 00:05:56.450
and the site at Filingdales is over 200 miles north of London, England,

00:05:56.490 --> 00:05:59.970
in a location that completes the northward coverage for...

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:06.820
ICBM over the North Pole and extends southeast detection down through Europe against a mid-continental

00:06:06.820 --> 00:06:13.570
missile attack. It also overlaps the west edge of the Thule BMU's radar. BMU's is fine for

00:06:13.570 --> 00:06:20.760
detecting missiles, but not for detecting bombers. Bombers can fly in undetected beneath the BMU's

00:06:20.760 --> 00:06:29.780
radar fan, but bombers can't get by the DU line undetected. DU stands for distant early

00:06:29.780 --> 00:06:29.980
you were

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:35.430
warning line the radars of the dew line are designed for low and high-level air traffic

00:06:35.430 --> 00:06:40.960
surveillance they are operated and maintained by the federal electric corporation through

00:06:41.010 --> 00:06:47.040
contract with the United States Air Force they are strategically placed along the Arctic Circle

00:06:47.040 --> 00:06:58.260
so that no bomber on an Arctic route can fly under around or over their search pattern from Alaska

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:08.910
wilderness of the north through Canada and over the 10,000 foot thick ice cap of

00:07:08.910 --> 00:07:14.860
Greenland more than 30 dew line sites form a fence of electronic eyes 5,000

00:07:14.860 --> 00:07:20.060
miles long on the eastern end it is tied into the surveillance systems of

00:07:20.060 --> 00:07:28.700
our NATO allies through Iceland to Norway no matter how isolated the site no

00:07:29.430 --> 00:07:29.870
matter how

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:36.360
long the Arctic days and nights around it, no matter how terrible the cold, every site of the

00:07:36.360 --> 00:07:43.400
dew and bimew systems is a place where men must live, work, and survive under some of the strangest

00:07:43.400 --> 00:07:49.860
conditions in the world. On the Greenland ice cap, some dew line buildings have to be jacked up as

00:07:49.860 --> 00:07:55.830
much as 10 feet a year to keep them above snow. The feet of the buildings are already 65 feet

00:07:55.830 --> 00:07:59.880
under snow and yet each year six more feet of snow pile

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:06.300
up and the buildings have to be jacked up again and again the buildings are five stories above

00:08:06.300 --> 00:08:12.260
the level of the snow so that the cold air can circulate underneath them if there were no cold

00:08:12.260 --> 00:08:17.540
air space underneath the building would melt the ice beneath it with its own heat and quickly

00:08:17.540 --> 00:08:29.870
disappear into the ice cap where buildings are built on permafrost the bottom of the building

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:36.310
have to be air conditioned to keep the heat from melting the permafrost in a land where the wind

00:08:36.310 --> 00:08:44.870
can jump from 15 to 150 miles per hour in a few minutes no man is safe wherever men travel there

00:08:44.870 --> 00:08:52.110
are emergency huts by the roadside called phase shacks these huts have a telephone emergency food

00:08:52.110 --> 00:08:58.820
rations and a gas stove when a man must go out in a severe arctic storm he must take a buddy with him

00:08:59.480 --> 00:08:59.880
No

00:09:00.090 --> 00:09:05.320
goes out alone then. The Wing Command Post has declared Thule Airbase to be in a

00:09:05.320 --> 00:09:10.370
Phase 3 condition. All personnel must be accounted for immediately. If you have

00:09:10.370 --> 00:09:13.590
been ordered to remain on duty, report your location to your barracks chief

00:09:13.590 --> 00:09:19.240
immediately. Thule Airbase is now in a Phase 3 condition. The alert is also given

00:09:19.240 --> 00:09:29.900
in Danish. This means that exposed flesh will freeze in 60 seconds. What kind of

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:36.520
protection does this demand. First, thermal underwear, double socks, and regular clothes.

00:09:37.620 --> 00:09:48.080
On top of that, mutlucks, quilted pants, mittens, parkas, and face masks. If a man omits any of

00:09:48.080 --> 00:09:53.340
these articles of clothing under these weather conditions, the Arctic winter in seconds can

00:09:53.340 --> 00:09:59.570
cripple or kill him. Survival is an iron discipline. One mistake and a man dies.

00:10:00.800 --> 00:10:06.420
doorknobs are plastic covered metal on a doorknob would freeze to the flesh of a man's hand

00:10:07.240 --> 00:10:13.440
under the worst conditions if the power failed at some sites even the men in the building could be

00:10:13.440 --> 00:10:21.420
frozen solid in 45 minutes 99 of the time there is no place to go except into the next room the

00:10:21.730 --> 00:10:29.160
men fight boredom as well as the cold maintenance men become amateur carpenters mechanics become

00:10:29.160 --> 00:10:29.860
sound expert.

00:10:31.760 --> 00:10:35.780
Electricians become lapidarists, polishing semi-precious stones.

00:10:37.260 --> 00:10:40.820
And some men even raise tropical fish, or try to.

00:10:47.120 --> 00:10:50.600
But the principal work is watching the sky toward the North Pole.

00:11:12.080 --> 00:11:29.300
This constant watch is kept at places called Sagleck, Melville at Goose Bay, Pinkersuit Mountain, Cape Dyer, but Arctic harbors are frozen solid for nine months out of the year.

00:11:30.990 --> 00:11:35.450
only in the summer can the coast guard and the navy keep them open with icebreakers

00:11:35.450 --> 00:11:42.420
on the voyage north the vessels break through the ice pack and pass 200 and 300 foot icebergs

00:11:43.430 --> 00:11:49.960
structural damage to reinforced hulls is common sometimes the ice pack will close upon a ship

00:11:51.200 --> 00:11:56.180
during whaling days many ships were trapped in the ice and crushed by tremendous pressure

00:11:56.180 --> 00:11:59.960
in three short months ships of the united

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:02.280
United States Military Sea Transport Service.

00:12:02.620 --> 00:12:05.420
must deliver most of the supplies for an entire year.

00:12:09.400 --> 00:12:13.660
The Army's 264th Transportation Company from Fort Eustis, Virginia,

00:12:14.230 --> 00:12:17.670
Supply Stevedor support for the unloading operation at Thule.

00:12:18.490 --> 00:12:19.450
Beginning in July,

00:12:19.930 --> 00:12:22.710
Approximately 200 men spend three months

00:12:23.000 --> 00:12:26.540
Unloading vessels that supply Thule Air Base and other sites.

00:12:27.000 --> 00:12:29.980
with everything from tea bags to 50-ton cranes.

00:12:40.080 --> 00:12:45.880
Every site has to be supplied with everything, eggs, antennas, and mail.

00:12:56.480 --> 00:12:59.220
Airlift must be used for the more remote sites.

00:13:00.060 --> 00:13:03.140
Aircraft operate from all types of landing services.

00:13:04.630 --> 00:13:09.890
At Hawthorne Naval Air Station, Iceland, a Navy C-47 must land on a gravel beach.

00:13:12.470 --> 00:13:15.090
Mail and supplies are then loaded on a fishing boat.

00:13:24.310 --> 00:13:25.990
After a trip across a small inlet,

00:13:26.330 --> 00:13:29.790
It'll be loaded onto trucks for the final 12 miles ride to the site.

00:13:30.000 --> 00:13:30.980
Thank you.

00:13:33.220 --> 00:13:34.140
At die three,

00:13:34.760 --> 00:13:38.000
Ski-equipped C-130s land on the Greenland Ice Cat.

00:13:38.980 --> 00:13:42.940
Every month of the year, the runway is an endless stretch of snow.

00:13:45.990 --> 00:13:49.630
It must be remembered that the eyes of the North form a defensive system.

00:13:49.960 --> 00:13:51.520
not an offensive system.

00:13:53.030 --> 00:13:58.770
The Air Defense Command of the United States Air Force supplies over 70% of the men and equipment.

00:13:59.140 --> 00:14:00.000
that make up our

00:14:00.000 --> 00:14:00.980
our eyes of the north.

00:14:01.620 --> 00:14:02.600
Thank you.

00:14:06.650 --> 00:14:09.450
including aircraft to intercept enemy bombers.

00:14:12.860 --> 00:14:16.880
The Navy has powerful anti-submarine forces patrolling the Arctic seas.

00:14:21.340 --> 00:14:22.940
These are defensive forces.

00:14:23.990 --> 00:14:26.970
But BMU's is our first line of warning in the north.

00:14:28.060 --> 00:14:29.440
If a missile threat occurs,

00:14:30.380 --> 00:14:32.640
Automatic transmission circuits take over.

00:14:45.960 --> 00:14:48.160
the BMU's rearward communications net,

00:14:48.460 --> 00:14:51.680
is operated by a number of military and civilian organizations.

00:14:52.870 --> 00:14:55.290
The Canadian Marconi Company, one of these,

00:14:55.820 --> 00:14:57.080
relays this information.

00:14:57.900 --> 00:14:59.860
information racing with an electronics

00:15:00.020 --> 00:15:00.660
Speed of light.

00:15:00.980 --> 00:15:03.140
From BMU sites at Clear, Alaska.

00:15:04.340 --> 00:15:05.160
Thule, Greenland.

00:15:05.820 --> 00:15:07.360
and Fidingdale's Moor, England,

00:15:08.150 --> 00:15:10.750
to the North American Air Defense Command, NORAD.

00:15:11.510 --> 00:15:15.930
the Underground Combat Operations Center located at Colorado Springs, Colorado.

00:15:20.410 --> 00:15:23.950
Voice communications back up this electronic radar warning.

