All BNews sites report in microseconds.

00:15:44.040 --> 00:15:48.100
over a communications net equivalent to twice the distance around the equator.

00:15:49.380 --> 00:15:50.300
At the dew line,

00:15:50.820 --> 00:15:53.000
Experienced eyes detect aircraft.

00:15:53.420 --> 00:15:55.600
by a blip on a dewline radar scope.

00:16:01.630 --> 00:16:07.810
at a similar scope at a direction center further south a team of professionals plot its course

00:16:07.810 --> 00:16:21.190
its approximate speed its altitude radar sightings are compared with known air traffic if the

00:16:21.190 --> 00:16:28.310
aircraft radar track fails to match a logged flight plan it is declared unknown norad combat

